    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d920">

                <pb facs="1037" n="1025" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/3266: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-21">June 21, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1461. American interests Hong Kong. Your 3258 May 28.<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d920-f1"/> Please endeavor to ascertain and report number of
                    Filipinos actually receiving financial assistance, as well as number considered
                    qualified to receive financial assistance under Department’s 249 of January 30,
                    960 of April 23 and 1292 of May 29 but not receiving financial assistance owing
                    to attitude of Japanese authorities.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d920-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d920-f1" n="30" xml:id="d920-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for summary, see footnote 28, <ref target="#pg1023">p.
                    1023</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d920-f2" n="31" xml:id="d920-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 4182, July 15, the Minister in Switzerland cited a report of the
                    Swiss Legation in Japan that 166 Filipinos had applied for relief and that
                    “Payment could be made to 77 but for Japanese prohibition payment funds
                    Filipinos who are not American citizens.” (340.1115A/3282)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
